        "answer": {
          "short": "Income tax: \\$102 439.60; Medicare levy: \\$5856.56; total tax: \\$108 296.16; monthly PAYG: \\$9024.68; monthly net income: \\$15 377.65.",
          "worked": "The taxable income is in the \\$180 001 and over bracket. There are 12 months in a year.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess}&=292\\,828-180\\,000\\\\\\text{Excess}&=112\\,828\\\\\\text{Income tax}&=51\\,667+0.45\\times112\\,828\\\\\\text{Income tax}&=\\$102\\,439.60\\\\\\text{Medicare levy}&=0.02\\times292\\,828\\\\\\text{Medicare levy}&=\\$5856.56\\\\\\text{Total tax}&=102\\,439.60+5856.56\\\\\\text{Total tax}&=\\$108\\,296.16\\\\\\text{Monthly PAYG}&=108\\,296.16\\div12\\\\\\text{Monthly PAYG}&=\\$9024.68\\\\\\text{Monthly gross}&=292\\,828\\div12\\\\\\text{Monthly gross}&\\approx\\$24\\,402.33\\\\\\text{Monthly net}&=24\\,402.33-9024.68\\\\\\text{Monthly net}&=\\$15\\,377.65\\end{align*}$$",
